  "criticalDistinctions": [
    "PALM: 1893 repeats Pueri antiphons; 1962 Roman chant owner's paired Psalm 23/46 verses must not be removed.",
    "CANDLEMAS: 1893 Exsurge is historically present after distribution, absent in the 1962 Roman source. The current reader is correct on this point.",
    "ROGATIONS: 1893 says participants rise and begin moving after the Sancta Maria invocation. Do not automatically shift 1962 posture trigger without a 1962 rubric.",
    "ROGATIONS: a Cantus prolixior proves this historical book has an alternate longer litany melody, NOT that any particular schola or 1962 celebration can use it.",
    "CORPUS: a feast section lists multiple hymns, but the explicitly local 'Lauda Sion' interpolation must not become automatic procession content.",
    "All stage/event IDs refer to already existing Ad Orientem source owners. Mapping historical context onto an event never certifies this 1893 chant as prescribed for that 1962 event."
  ],
